-- DB update 2026_09_10_05 -> 2026_09_10_06
-- Arcane Mage rework (docs/arcane-mage-rework-design.md) - Phase 3, Batch A.
-- .claude/skills/class-rework/SKILL.md Phase 3: MageMechanics.cpp percent-damage-done hooks for 3
-- of the "Deferred to Phase 3" list's clauses (see plan at the time:
-- ~/.claude/plans/twinkling-strolling-lagoon.md).
--
-- Data half of this batch: adds a SPELL_AURA_DUMMY marker effect (read live in
-- MageMechanics.cpp::ApplyDoneDamagePctMods via the marker-aura-by-icon idiom) to already-shipped
-- Phase 2 talent rank spells - no talent_dbc changes, no new spell ids, just one new effect slot per
-- row carrying the ranked bonus %:
--   Arcane Resonance (3,2), talent 1142, ranks 18462/18463/18464: effect1 was already an inert
--     SPELL_AURA_DUMMY shell (base_points 0) from Phase 2 - given its real ranked value (3/6/9%).
--   Arcane Mind (4,3), talent 77, ranks 11232/12500/12501: new effect2 (SPELL_AURA_DUMMY, 4/8/12%
--     max, scaled live by current mana% in C++ - grows with mana, confirmed with the user).
--   Arcane Flows (7,1), talent 1843, rank 2 only (44379, the capstone rank): new effect3
--     (SPELL_AURA_DUMMY, flat 5%).
--
-- C++ half (src/server/game/Entities/Unit/MageMechanics.cpp, src/server/scripts/Spells/
-- spell_mage.cpp) ships alongside this migration, not through generate.py - see that diff.
--
-- Also relocated: spell 36032 ("Arcane Blast" stacking self-buff, real stock data) from
-- source/spells/npc.csv to source/spells/mage.csv - pull.py's file-guess heuristic misfiled it
-- there (same pattern as earlier batches), corrected now since several Phase 3 items read its live
-- stack count. Content untouched, reference-only, produces no DBC diff (confirmed via generate.py
-- before this batch's marker edits were added).
--
-- Not yet done this batch (moved to Batch C, see plan): the Missile Barrage/Arcane Concentration
-- shared Mastery clause - closer reading of Spell::finish()'s RemoveSpellMods timing showed a
-- channeled-spell risk (Arcane Missiles' Clearcasting/Missile-Barrage-proc consumption happens at
-- channel start, before any tick's damage calc), so a naive live HasAura() read in
-- ApplyDoneDamagePctMods would silently never fire for Missiles. Needs the same signal-flag pattern
-- already used by the existing T10 2P bonus tie-in (spell_mage_missile_barrage_proc::OnRemove ->
-- spell_mage_arcane_missiles), which belongs with Missile Barrage's other proc-mechanism work.
--
-- generate.py clean (zero lint WARNINGs). codestyle-cpp.py clean on both edited C++ files (repo-wide
-- pre-existing findings elsewhere are unrelated). test_sql_dump.py + manual balanced-statement scan
-- clean - codestyle-sql.py itself can't run in this sandbox (no network for git fetch), same
-- accepted limitation as every prior batch.

